   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0",
   "html": "<p>In a particular semiconductor, the electron concentration is constant and equal to 5 × 10<sup>15</sup> cm<sup>–3</sup>.<br />\nGiven hole concentration changes with <em>x</em> as</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/19dab6a3c94f7a273535.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>where, <em>L</em> = 12 mm. Hole diffusion coefficient is <em>D<sub>p</sub></em> = 12 cm<sup>2</sup>/s.<br />\nElectron mobility, μ<em><sub>n</sub></em> = 1000 cm<sup>2</sup>/V-s.<br />\nTotal current density, <em>J</em> = 4.5 A/cm<sup>2</sup>.<br />\nThen the electric field at x = 10 μm is equal to _______ kV/m. (upto two decimal places)</div>",
